BEFORE TABLE: Cal. Code Regs. Tit. 14, § 5.00 - Black Bass State Regulations Compare It is unlawful to take or possess black bass except as provided in this section: (Note: Some waters are closed to all fishing under Sections 7.40 and 7.50 .) (a) General Statewide Restrictions: (1) Lakes/Reservoirs and the Sacramento-San Joaquin Delta: The following waters, except for those listed in subsection (b), are open to fishing all year, with a 12-inch total length minimum size limit and a five-fish daily bag limit: All lakes and reservoirs in the State, and the Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta (see Section 1.71 for definition of the Delta). (2) Rivers/Streams and Private Ponds: Rivers, streams, canals, and lakes or ponds entirely on private lands that are not listed in subsection (b) are open all year with no size limit and a five-fish daily bag limit. (b) Special Regulations: Counties and individual waters listed below are those having regulations different from the General Statewide Restrictions in subsection (a). DISTRICTS AND COUNTIES WITH SPECIAL REGULATIONS
